FAIL seat guide holds only retained rules and the brief checklist ["- In Claude Code, launch each builder, reviewer or role child as a background task and end your turn. In pi, run it as one foreground command with no timeout.","- Start scout (code scouting and research gathering), planner and adversary through `pi-worker --slot <slot> --brief <file> --out <file>`. Node form: `node \"$HOME/nana-pi/packages/nana-pack/bin/pi-worker.mjs\" --slot <slot> --brief <file> --out <file>`; PowerShell: `node \"$env:USERPROFILE\\nana-pi\\packages\\nana-pack\\bin\\pi-worker.mjs\" --slot <slot> --brief <file> --out <file>`. A role whose roster line reads `seat` or `none` runs in the seat. Scout and planner launches are the seat's choice; use an adversary once per plan. Read lineage warnings; change a shared or unverified slot rather than silently substituting another model.","- While a builder or reviewer runs, do not read or judge its partial output, transcript, diffs or test results. Do not re-run its checks before it ends.","- Leave a running builder or reviewer alone until its completion notification arrives or a monitor reports a failure or a stall. Then act in that turn.","- Before pushing a lane branch, run `node \"$HOME/nana-pi/packages/nana-pack/bin/leak-scan.mjs\" --base main --tip HEAD` chained with `&&` to the push; on a hit, fix the commit before any push.","- Verify once, when the build ends. Re-run the seat checks your brief names, read the builder's report, and look at every page or command output the change produces.","- On a lane that produces or changes a page a person looks at, run first-look after build 1 and save the shots outside git: `npm run first-look -- --page product --out <folder>`, `--page desk --before <url> --after <url>`, or, for a new page or one with a reference, `--page url --after <url> --reference <folder> --spec <file> --out <folder>`. Point the owner to the shots with one question: is this the shape?","- On a lane that changes the product page, after first-look run `npm run outside-reader -- --from <first-look folder> --out <folder>` outside git, show the owner its top new finding in your report, and write a known-bug line only for a finding that is a real defect.","- On a lane whose page has a reference, run `npm run visual-reader -- --from <first-look folder> --out <folder>` outside git before you point the owner to the shots. Point the owner to them only after it prints a pass, or after you have judged them side by side with the reference yourself and say so in your report.","- On a lane that builds or reshapes a page a person looks at, write the build brief from `$HOME/nana-pi/docs/ui-brief-template.md`. The seat picks references by default. The owner's starred references from the library replace those picks when the owner wants a say.","- Every lane gets one reviewer plus CI.","- Send findings on a build back in the next brief instead of fixing the builder's work yourself.","- Before you end your turn, name and start what waits on nothing else: another lane's build, separate research agents. Each lane's own steps stay in order.","- Run the full suite whole, never in parts. Never split a long run while a full suite runs on the same machine. If a check fails on a time limit, re-run it alone before you call it a failure.","- Keep no more lanes building than the lanes line of this machine's roster command allows, `node \"$HOME/nana-pi/packages/nana-pack/bin/nana-roster.mjs\"`, and at most two more in planning. A lane in planning has no build yet and no builder working in it. A lane counts as building from its first build until it lands or closes.","- The builder preamble holds the builder's rules and the review standard holds the reviewer's. Judge review findings by the review standard, and restate neither in a brief.","- On an enabled personal machine, automatically save quoted preferences, corrections, facts and thinking about the owner to both the private profile and today's shared memory until delivery lands. Run `node \"$HOME/nana-pi/packages/nana-pack/bin/nana-profile.mjs\" save`; never enable saving on a machine without the owner's choice. Show each Saved: line in your reply so the owner can retract it; confirm only on an explicit owner yes with new owner words. Never save as a builder or reviewer, from a linked worktree, or from a disabled machine. Decisions belong in nana-rulings.md and open threads in GitHub issues."]
